                <pb facs="0416" n="330" sameAs="frus:frus1927v01/pg330"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">717.2114/53: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Munro</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-10-04T14:00:00-05:45"><hi rendition="#italic">October 4,
                                1927—2 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 5:15 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>260. Department’s May [<hi rendition="#italic">September</hi>] 14, 5 p.m. The
                    President asked me today to ascertain when the Department would be ready to
                    express an opinion regarding the San Andrés Archipelago question.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Munro</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
